    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Florida-Institute-of-Technology/School-of-Arts-and-Communication-Post-Doc-Visiting-Research-Associate_R9285": {
      "title": "School of Arts and Communication Post Doc Visiting Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Arts and Communication at Florida Institute of Technology seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate as an active participant in the project “Cultivating Core Character through the General Education Core,” funded by Wake Forest University and the Lilly Endowment Inc. under co-PIs Lars Jones, Andrew Aberdein, and Heidi Hatfield Edwards. Beyond pursuing their own research agenda, the successful candidate will work under the supervision of project PIs and is expected to begin the 12-month annual position in January 2027 and continue through the end of the grant term in July 2029. Funds available for approved grant-related travel. Salary supplements may also be available.        Specific responsibilities will include:   ·       Teaching up to or the equivalent of two core undergraduate courses directly tied to our character education framework, ensuring pedagogical fidelity and integration with project goals.   ·       Partnering with the PIs to support faculty and student virtue-education training, including workshops, mentoring, classroom sessions, and follow-up engagement.   ·       Supporting the PIs in university-wide advocacy and outreach to other colleges as well as to the broader public.   ·       Assisting the lead PI in designing and leading the biweekly character colloquium (topic selection, readings, integration with curriculum).   ·       Attending weekly project team meetings.   ·       Contributing to assessment planning, execution, and review to enable a rigorous evaluation of student and faculty outcomes.   ·       Coordinating implementation and analysis of the project’s diagnostic framework, ensuring consistent data collection, interpretation, and integration across participating courses.   ·       Collaborating on pedagogical scholarship tied to project activities and outputs, in addition to advancing their own research agenda.   ·       Working with in-house support units, as well as student assistants, to help the PIs develop four Canvas LMS modules for scalable character education use in the University and beyond.      Qualifications   The successful candidate must have:   ·       A PhD (either awarded or submitted and with defense formally scheduled) in a humanistic discipline, with a research specialization related to character education and/or virtue theory.   ·       Demonstrated strong interest and ability in teaching.   ·       Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills.   ·       Ability to work both independently and as part of a team that must deal professionally with people at all levels.      Preference will be given for those candidates who have applied character education experience and/or a substantive specialization in virtue theory, complemented by demonstrated pedagogical skill.    The successful candidate will participate in implementing and expanding our program across the instructional, developmental, and scholarly domains rather than acting only as a pure research scholar.   Informal queries should be directed to character@fit.edu   Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities. The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following website 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Florida-Tech-Main-Campus-Melbourne/Associate-Director-of-Sponsored-Programs_R9524": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Sponsored Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Associate Director of Sponsored Research supports the development, submission, administration, and oversight of the university's sponsored research and other externally funded programs. Working closely with the Director, faculty, administrators, and external sponsors, this position provides leadership across the full grant and contract lifecycle, including proposal development, award management, compliance, financial monitoring, reporting, and closeout. The Associate Director serves as a resource to faculty and staff on sponsored program processes and requirements, ensures compliance with applicable regulations and policies, and supports strategic initiatives, budget oversight, and continuous improvement efforts to advance the university's research mission. Responsibilities Include: Sponsored Programs Administration Assist in the oversight and administration of sponsored research and other externally funded programs throughout the full award lifecycle, including proposal development, submission, award acceptance, modifications, compliance monitoring, and closeout. Ensure compliance with sponsor requirements, Uniform Guidance, federal and state regulations, and university policies and procedures. Review grant and contract proposals and budgets for accuracy, completeness, and adherence to sponsor and institutional requirements. Provide guidance and training to faculty, principal investigators, and departmental staff on sponsored program administration, proposal development, and compliance requirements. Serve as a subject matter expert and resource for pre-award and post-award activities. Research Reporting and Systems Support Compile, analyze, and report data related to proposal submissions, awards, expenditures, and other research performance metrics. Support the administration, optimization, and continuous improvement of research administration systems and business processes. Develop reports, dashboards, and other tools to support sponsored project management, compliance, and institutional decision-making. Project Management and Strategic Initiatives Serve as project manager for major sponsored research, compliance, and institutional initiatives. Coordinate activities across multiple departments and stakeholders, monitor project progress, manage risks, and communicate updates to leadership. Support strategic initiatives that enhance research administration services, strengthen institutional research capacity, and improve operational effectiveness. Qualifications Required: Bachelor's degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Three (3) or more years of progressively responsible experience in research administration, grants management, sponsored programs, or a related field. Knowledge of federal regulations, Uniform Guidance, sponsor requirements, and research administration best practices. Strong project management, analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, sponsors, and senior leadership. Preferred Experience in both pre-award and post-award research administration within a higher education environment. Experience with research administration and enterprise systems, including Workday Grants, Cayuse, or similar grants management platforms. Experience developing reports, dashboards, and business process improvements. Professional certification such as Certified Research Administrator (CRA), Certified Financial Research Administrator (CFRA), or related credential. Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities. The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following website 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Florida-Tech-Main-Campus-Melbourne/Research-Scientist---CCE_R9440": {
      "title": "Research Scientist - CCE",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nBiochar Research and Innovation Laboratory is seeking applications for a research scientist, who will primarily assist the required tasks associated with a newly funded FDEP project on Quick Reef demonstration for nutrient removal from Indian River Lagoon. Job Responsibilities: Develop Quality Assurance Project Plan Develop permitting paperwork Perform analysis at the NELAP labs Advise students, develop reports, and disseminate results to the public and management Requirements: PhD in Chemical Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or relevant field. Prior experience on quality assurance project plan development. Minimum of 2-5 years of experience required in area of expertise. Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities. The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following website 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Florida-Tech-Main-Campus-Melbourne/Cook-Cashier_R9522": {
      "title": "Cook/Cashier",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCook/Cashier Florida Tech Main Campus Melbourne Dining location: Rathskeller Pizza & Grill Operating hours: 4:00pm to 11:30pm daily Come join the team at the late-night hot spot on campus! Working in an open kitchen, cook to order concept, preparing hot and cold menu items from fresh and frozen state. The duties include opening set-up and closing procedures for pizza making equipment, fryer and flat top grill stations. Must maintain standards that ensure food safety and presentation, quality, cleanliness, in a fast paced, challenging environment. Also, may be required to operate our POS register system, take customer orders and deliver food around the campus community. All team members are required to assist in maintaining dining room cleanliness, restock the convenient store shelving and drink display coolers. Responsibilities: May be asked to work at another Campus Dining location as needed The position is typically in our Rathskeller Pizza and Grill quick service, grocery, snack bar and pizza delivery operation and is accountable for following standardized recipes. Operating the cash register according to specified procedures, taking customer orders and maintaining the kitchen area to meet sanitation, health and safety standards. Properly rotate perishable ingredients, utilize code date labeling to ensure the highest quality menu items are served. Performs routine cleaning and organization of workstations, equipment, all food production and food storage areas of the operation. Requirements: Candidate possessing a current / valid driver’s license are preferred, as this enables them to drive University vehicles for the purpose of food deliveries to the campus community. Must be able to stand for extended periods of time in a fast-paced work environment. Education High School Diploma or GED preferred.  Education and work experience in the food service or similar industry has valued merit Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities. The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following website 2025 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
